message: "If you use or discuss this theory, please cite the foundation paper below."
title: "Sector Causality Theory: when does self-duality cause physics?"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Callens
    given-names: Xavier
    affiliation: SocrateAI Research
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/xaviercallens/SocrateAI-Scientific-SectorCausalityTheory"
abstract: >-
  The dedicated home of the Sector Causality Theory: a criterion stating that a self-dual point is
  forced to be physically distinguished if and only if it exchanges two inequivalent sectors on a
  discrete fixed-point set. Contains the foundation paper and its two companion papers, a
  self-contained Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization (116 kernel-checked theorems across 14 modules,
  re-verified by a second independent kernel), reproduction notebooks, and an MCP server exposing the
  theory's case table and theorems to scientists and AI agents.
keywords: [duality, self-duality, topological sectors, phase transitions, Lean 4, Mathlib, formal verification, interventionist causation, Model Context Protocol]
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "When does self-duality cause physics? A machine-checked criterion, tested across sixteen candidate physical systems, an interventional experiment, and real cosmological data"
